'''HICL Infrastructure Company''' (formerly '''HSBC Infrastructure Company Ltd''') is a large [[United Kingdom|British]] [[investment company]] dedicated to infrastructure investments. It is listed on the [[London Stock Exchange]] and it is a constituent of the [[FTSE 250 Index]]. The company is managed by InfraRed Capital Partners<ref name="citywire1"/><ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.morningstar.co.uk/uk/news/AN_1458285939410761900/hicl-infrastructure-to-raise-gbp25-million-through-tap-issuance-(alliss).aspx |title=HICL Infrastructure To Raise GBP25 Million Through... |publisher=Morningstar |date=18 March 2016 |access-date=6 March 2017 |archive-date=7 March 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170307045837/http://www.morningstar.co.uk/uk/news/AN_1458285939410761900/hicl-infrastructure-to-raise-gbp25-million-through-tap-issuance-(alliss).aspx |url-status=dead }}</ref> and the [[chairman]] is Mike Bane.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.morningstar.co.uk/uk/news/AN_1732098160861821900/hicl-infrastructure-reports-profit-recovery-and-confirms-dividend-goal.aspx |title=HICL Infrastructure reports profit recovery and confirms dividend goal |date=20 November 2024 |newspaper=Morning Star |access-date=25 November 2024}}</ref>

==History==
The company was established in 2006.<ref name="citywire1">{{cite web |last=Levy |first=Danielle |url=http://citywire.co.uk/money/hicl-share-offer-4-9-yield-at-a-smaller-premium/a995398 |title=HICL share offer: 4.9% yield at a smaller premium |publisher=Citywire.co.uk |date=27 February 2017 |access-date=6 March 2017}}</ref> In November 2025, it was announced that the assets of [[The Renewables Infrastructure Group]] would be transferred to HICL Infrastructure Company and that The Renewables Infrastructure Group would subsequently be wound up.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.reuters.com/business/hicl-renewables-infrastructure-combine-form-uks-largest-listed-infra-firm-2025-11-17/  |title=HICL, Renewables Infrastructure to combine into $5.2 billion UK-listed infrastructure firm |date=17 November 2025 |newspaper=Reuters |access-date=18 November 2025}}</ref> After a shareholder revolt, the proposed transaction was abandoned in December 2025.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://portfolio-adviser.com/hicl-trig-merger-called-off-after-shareholder-revolt/ |title=HICL-TRIG merger called off after shareholder revolt |newspaper=Portfolio Adviser |date=1 December 2025 |access-date=4 December 2025}}</ref>

==Operations==
The company is focused on three segments: [[public–private partnership]] (PPP) and [[private finance initiative]] (PFI) (social and transport projects), regulated assets (gas and electricity transmission and distribution, and water utilities) and demand-based assets (such as toll road concessions and student accommodation).<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.hl.co.uk/news/articles/hicl-infrastructure-company-limited-on-track-to-raise-dividend-ahead-of-inflation |title=HICL Infrastructure Company Limited - on track to raise dividend ahead of inflation |date=18 November 2016 |publisher=Hl.co.uk |access-date=6 March 2017}}</ref> Portfolio Investments are located primarily in the United Kingdom, but also in Australia, North America and Europe<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.bestinvest.co.uk/news/hicl-infrastructure-new-fund-raising |title=HICL Infrastructure – new fund raising |publisher=Bestinvest.co.uk |access-date=6 March 2017}}</ref> and investments are generally operational.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.investorschronicle.co.uk/2016/11/03/funds-and-etfs/top-100-funds/hicl-expanding-beyond-ppp-assets-into-toll-roads-05XXIDorZmu2e1Q6mXKr2N/article.html |title=HICL expanding beyond PPP assets into toll roads |publisher=Investors Chronicle |access-date=6 March 2017}}</ref>

